# Inference engines to compare with the SAME model file. One engine per line:
#   id | base URL (with /v1) | model name the endpoint expects | start command | stop command
# Start/stop run through `sh -c`; "-" means the engine is already running (not started or stopped
# by run.sh). This file is trusted input: only put commands here that you would run yourself.
# Copy to engines.conf and edit. The model should be the same GGUF everywhere (see docs/local-llm.md).

# llama.cpp through kit-llm, default threads vs. 4 threads
llamacpp|http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1|qwen3.5-2b|kit-llm start qwen3.5-2b|kit-llm stop
llamacpp-4t|http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1|qwen3.5-2b|KIT_LLM_THREADS=4 kit-llm start qwen3.5-2b|kit-llm stop

# A second llama.cpp build (for example a newer release unpacked by hand) on another port:
# llamacpp-new|http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1|m|KIT_LLM_SERVER=$HOME/llama-new/llama-server KIT_LLM_PORT=8081 kit-llm start qwen3.5-2b|KIT_LLM_PORT=8081 kit-llm stop

# Ollama, if IT allows it and it is already running with the same GGUF imported
# (Modelfile: FROM /path/to/Qwen3.5-2B-Q4_K_M.gguf; ollama create kit-qwen3.5-2b -f Modelfile):
# ollama|http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1|kit-qwen3.5-2b|-|-
